1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,058
Every trader has their own way of reading a chart.

2
00:00:02,808 --> 00:00:05,754
Angstrom Lattice lets you write yours down once,

3
00:00:05,854 --> 00:00:08,301
and have it checked on every asset you follow.

4
00:00:08,791 --> 00:00:10,432
It starts with signals:

5
00:00:10,182 --> 00:00:14,909
the indicators behind the dashboard, such as moving averages, RSI, volume,

6
00:00:14,659 --> 00:00:16,179
and market structure.

7
00:00:15,929 --> 00:00:17,873
Each one measures one thing.

8
00:00:18,356 --> 00:00:21,256
Signal Groups combine signals into one reading,

9
00:00:21,006 --> 00:00:24,131
a score from minus one hundred to plus one hundred,

10
00:00:24,231 --> 00:00:26,655
with labels you choose, such as Bullish.

11
00:00:26,405 --> 00:00:31,436
The dashboard's already configured Trend, Stretch and Flow are Signal Groups like these.

12
00:00:31,927 --> 00:00:34,609
Signal Sets turn readings into a decision:

13
00:00:34,709 --> 00:00:36,452
Yes, No, or Unknown,

14
00:00:36,552 --> 00:00:40,514
with the line that decided it. For example: the trend is bullish,

15
00:00:40,614 --> 00:00:44,107
and RSI is at most forty, a pullback in an uptrend.

16
00:00:44,592 --> 00:00:47,317
Prism Scan runs a Set across your watchlist,

17
00:00:47,417 --> 00:00:48,413
now,

18
00:00:48,513 --> 00:00:50,150
at a past moment,

19
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:51,801
or on a schedule.

20
00:00:52,296 --> 00:00:54,978
And when an asset turns Yes, you hear about it,

21
00:00:55,078 --> 00:00:57,440
instantly or in your daily summary.

22
00:00:57,975 --> 00:01:02,492
Strategies come next: entries, exits, and risk, built on the same Sets.

23
00:01:02,977 --> 00:01:06,000
Why it helps: your rules stay the same every time,

24
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,292
every answer shows its reasons,

25
00:01:08,392 --> 00:01:11,756
and missing data is reported as Unknown, never guessed.

26
00:01:12,498 --> 00:01:15,244
Everything here describes the market as it is.

27
00:01:15,344 --> 00:01:17,834
It is not a forecast, and not advice.
